    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1943046129379336277",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1943046129379336277",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1943046129379336277",
      "text": "[9:30PM] #Idumota #TrafficUpdate \n\nThe traffic situation in Idumota, has undergone a significant transformation, with traffic finally subsiding after a period of congestion. As of now, movement within the area is very encouraging, and commuters can expect a relatively smooth journey.\n\nTwo key routes in the area are experiencing good traffic movement. The stretch from Adeniji Adele Road to 3rd Mainland Bridge is moving smoothly, allowing commuters to traverse this route without significant delays. Additionally, the route from Lubinrin to Carter Bridge is witnessing fast moving traffic, which is a welcome development for motorists.\n\nThe traffic flow on Carter Bridge, particularly inward journey towards Eyin Eyo, is good, with vehicles moving at a steady pace. Furthermore, the section from underneath Idumota Bridge to Carter Bridge is also experiencing good traffic movement, indicating effective traffic management.\n\nThe presence of traffic personnel on ground is playing a crucial role in maintaining the smooth traffic flow. These personnel are actively managing traffic, directing vehicles, and ensuring that the flow of traffic remains uninterrupted. Their efforts are yielding positive results, and commuters are benefiting from the efficient traffic management.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
